   THE PLANES THAT MEET IN BOTH CASES, by slope (azimuth in degrees, negative east of south):
   slope  0: both none                             typical only none
   slope 10: both none                             typical only -30, -15, +0, +15, +30, +45
   slope 20: both -15, +0, +15                     typical only -45, -30, +30, +45
   slope 30: both -15, +0, +15, +30                typical only -45, -30, +45
   slope 40: both -15, +0, +15, +30                typical only -30, +45
   slope 50: both -15, +0, +15                     typical only -30, +30, +45
   slope 60: both +0, +15                          typical only -15, +30
   slope 70: both none                             typical only +0, +15
   flat (slope 0): typical NOT MET, adverse NOT MET
   The 15 degree steps of the grid are the resolution: a plane between two grid points that both meet is not itself run.
